{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"id":"M-Igashi.mp3rgain","latestVersion":"3.16.2","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"M-Igashi","description":"Lossless MP3/AAC volume adjustment - a modern mp3gain / aacgain replacement written in Rust","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/blob/master/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"M-Igashi","description":"Lossless MP3/AAC volume adjustment - a modern mp3gain / aacgain replacement written in Rust","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/blob/master/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"mp3rgain changes the volume of MP3 and AAC (M4A/MP4 and raw ADTS) files without re-encoding, by rewriting the global_gain field stored in each frame, so audio quality is preserved.\nIt analyzes track and album loudness with ReplayGain 1.0 by default (mp3gain-identical values), or ReplayGain 2.0 and EBU R128 as options, writes REPLAYGAIN_* tags, and stores an undo tag that -u uses to revert gain changes.\nThe command-line options, TSV output and undo tag follow mp3gain, so existing scripts keep working.","moniker":"mp3rgain","name":"mp3rgain","packageUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain","publisher":"M-Igashi","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/releases/tag/v3.16.2","tags":["audio","cli","flac","gain","lossless","mp3","music","normalize","ogg","replaygain","rust","volume"]}},"longDescription":"mp3rgain changes the volume of MP3 and AAC (M4A/MP4 and raw ADTS) files without re-encoding, by rewriting the global_gain field stored in each frame, so audio quality is preserved.\nIt analyzes track and album loudness with ReplayGain 1.0 by default (mp3gain-identical values), or ReplayGain 2.0 and EBU R128 as options, writes REPLAYGAIN_* tags, and stores an undo tag that -u uses to revert gain changes.\nThe command-line options, TSV output and undo tag follow mp3gain, so existing scripts keep working.","moniker":"mp3rgain","name":"mp3rgain","packageUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain","publisher":"M-Igashi","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/M-Igashi/mp3rgain/releases/tag/v3.16.2","tags":["audio","cli","flac","gain","lossless","mp3","music","normalize","ogg","replaygain","rust","volume"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.16.2/app.json","detailSha256":"0754208e919452bc2cf55da3ea9f1b13a5016c0bfa2cd71fbd26fc87db5ee4a6","releaseDate":"2026-11-11","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"3.16.2"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.16.1/app.json","detailSha256":"75df8c5c2f1bfd4294f0133eb595304a919d12637304b4f543bc381cfe45259a","releaseDate":"2026-11-09","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"3.16.1"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.16.0/app.json","detailSha256":"2aefb01e5c22bece455e582d365ed08ccb9921c8cd0b08b0e77a58b02e759a2d","releaseDate":"2026-11-09","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"3.16.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.15.0/app.json","detailSha256":"ef3552d7607f05f26aff2aa0c601dc78008a91b45c23698d52fe1f9c467a9c50","releaseDate":"2026-10-30","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"3.15.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.14.0/app.json","detailSha256":"82142cd7bae9bed98c74386d702faaf61ee700309aeac42cc459990694688b87","releaseDate":"2026-10-27","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"3.14.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/3.13.0/app.json","detailSha256":"8d2a10dd2605220366b6dfa389a8d56d5b8ec9353370e93242ceb72952279020","releaseDate":"2026-10-25","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"3.13.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"ve